 === Biases in content ===
 
+Bias occurs in LLMs based upon what the LLM was trained to do or the training data the LLM trained upon. One reason LLMs are biased is their training data (e.g. an LLM's bias being skewed towards occidental countries due to training on data primarily originating from western sources). Many other factors play role, such as the manner the LLM model was designed in, or their systems of prioritization. Another factor may be AI hallucinations from less knowledge of a lesser-spoken and used vernacular (such as the Azerbaijani language).
+
 
 ==== Pro-authoritarian bias ====
-Even large American frontier AI models have for a number of prompts (as of 2026) a pro-authoritarian bias, due in part to how it is trained on the entirety of the internet (and does not exclude unreliable sources on political topics such as propaganda from state media). Model makers also cite safety for their users in authoritarian countries as another reason. Chinese language responses are also more authoritarian than English-language ones, for example. Models were also more likely to criticize governments in freer countries than more repressive regimes, sometimes citing safety concerns.
